## 15. Roles and Responsibilities (RACI)

The following RACI model may be referenced within runbooks where appropriate.

| Activity          | Operations | Platform Engineer | Service Owner | Change Manager |
| ----------------- | :--------: | :---------------: | :-----------: | :------------: |
| Execute Procedure |      R     |         A         |       I       |        I       |
| Review Procedure  |      C     |         R         |       A       |        I       |
| Approve Changes   |      I     |         C         |       C       |        A       |
| Document Results  |      R     |         C         |       I       |        I       |

Legend:

* **R** – Responsible
* **A** – Accountable
* **C** – Consulted
* **I** – Informed

---

## 16. Severity Levels

Operational incidents should be categorized using standardized severity levels.

| Severity | Description                | Example                       |
| -------- | -------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| Critical | Complete service outage    | Cluster unavailable           |
| High     | Major degradation          | Storage redundancy lost       |
| Medium   | Limited operational impact | Backup warning                |
| Low      | Minor issue                | Documentation update required |

Severity definitions may be adapted to organizational requirements.

---

## 17. Continuous Improvement

Operational documentation is considered a living asset.

Runbooks should be reviewed after:

* Major infrastructure changes
* Significant incidents
* Disaster recovery exercises
* Operational audits
* Lessons learned workshops

Feedback from operators should be incorporated into future revisions to improve clarity, accuracy, and operational effectiveness.

---

## 18. Public Repository Statement

This repository is intended for educational and demonstration purposes.

All examples are anonymized and do not represent any production environment.

The project intentionally excludes:

* Credentials
* Customer information
* Internal network details
* Production hostnames
* IP addresses
* Security-sensitive configurations
* Confidential operational procedures

